WEBVTT

00:20.020 --> 00:21.000
The next phrase...

00:43.330 --> 00:46.370
--Is that Yuki Ogata's daughter?!
--Yeah, it's her!

00:46.460 --> 00:49.420
--The future star!
--This is her first leading role!

01:09.820 --> 01:10.500
Rin...!

01:16.070 --> 01:20.660
<i>The world changes.</i>
<i>Almost like a scene change in a play...</i>

01:23.450 --> 01:25.830
<i>The year is 2025.</i>

01:25.910 --> 01:31.710
<i>A resistance group called the GGP</i>
<i>suddenly took control of the world.</i>

01:32.800 --> 01:37.010
<i>Standing up to the superpowers</i>
<i>was like an ant fighting an elephant,</i>

01:37.090 --> 01:40.930
<i>but the GGP's use of new</i>
<i>military capabilities changed all that</i>

01:41.010 --> 01:43.290
<i>and led it to its historical victory.</i>

01:44.180 --> 01:51.480
<i>These unseen heroes, now synonymous</i>
<i>with the term "historical victory,"</i>

01:51.570 --> 01:54.610
<i>abruptly vanished from the center stage.</i>

01:55.940 --> 02:00.530
<i>A new order and design for</i>
<i>the world came afterward.</i>

02:00.620 --> 02:03.030
<i>Military force that only intensified hatred.</i>

02:03.120 --> 02:06.620
<i>The ever-growing vicious cycle of revenge.</i>

02:06.710 --> 02:09.100
<i>Gray skies devoid of hope.</i>

02:10.380 --> 02:13.920
<i>Revolution. New order.</i>

02:14.000 --> 02:19.950
<i>But none of it meant anything to me.</i>
<i>Not even this changing world.</i>

02:22.470 --> 02:26.390
<i>All that mattered was that I follow my mother's advice</i>

02:26.480 --> 02:31.270
<i>and use my natural born gift as</i>
<i>a dancer to live life to the fullest.</i>

02:44.660 --> 02:46.990
<i>This is my world.</i>

02:47.080 --> 02:49.910
<i>This light, this sensation...</i>

02:50.000 --> 02:54.880
<i>It's only when I'm on stage that I really feel alive!</i>

03:37.460 --> 03:39.490
<i>Suddenly, the curtains were closed...</i>

03:44.140 --> 03:46.850
<i>The world changes...</i>

05:23.110 --> 05:24.630
Ready... go!

05:25.900 --> 05:29.990
--This is amazing!
--It's raining cherry blossoms!

05:30.080 --> 05:32.030
Do you think we're being too happy?

05:32.120 --> 05:33.660
Don't be silly!

05:33.750 --> 05:35.660
We start a new life today!

05:35.750 --> 05:38.540
And, by some miracle,
we're in the same dorm room!

05:38.630 --> 05:40.670
How can we not be excited?!

05:40.750 --> 05:42.000
Good point.

05:42.090 --> 05:45.210
Only eight minutes from
the train station, near a convenience store,

05:45.300 --> 05:47.510
separate bathroom and washroom, newly remodeled,

05:47.590 --> 05:50.180
and 160 square feet of space!

05:50.260 --> 05:54.180
Are you forgetting that
there'll be two beds and two desks?

05:54.270 --> 05:56.770
Oh, right. It might actually be cramped...

05:56.850 --> 06:00.310
Plus there's no air conditioning.
What do we do during the summer?!

06:00.400 --> 06:04.730
It'll be fine.
People have lived there before.

06:04.820 --> 06:07.110
It'll all work out!

06:07.200 --> 06:09.160
If you say so...

06:12.950 --> 06:14.910
It's so pretty...!

06:32.350 --> 06:37.060
Our country's turmoil was quieted
by the hard work of your parents

06:37.140 --> 06:41.520
and the reconstruction assistance from the GGP.

06:42.270 --> 06:47.070
It is my hope that what you learn at this school

06:47.150 --> 06:51.320
will help to create an even better society...

06:52.280 --> 06:57.830
Yes! The cherry blossoms are in
full bloom! They were beautiful!

06:57.910 --> 07:01.710
Most of them have fallen off the trees here.

07:01.790 --> 07:04.800
How are things there? How's Kenji?

07:05.020 --> 07:09.190
Anti-GGP group protests
arrival of aircraft carrier

07:07.010 --> 07:09.590
He hasn't come by at all.

07:09.670 --> 07:11.300
He still hasn't come back?

07:11.380 --> 07:15.100
He's a boy in puberty.
I can understand why he'd feel cramped

07:15.180 --> 07:17.350
in a house with just a senior citizen and a dog.

07:17.430 --> 07:18.310
Sheesh...

07:18.390 --> 07:21.940
This house is too big for only two people.

07:22.020 --> 07:26.650
It's easy enough to go out for lunch,
but at dinner it's just me and Peron.

07:26.730 --> 07:28.280
It gets very lonely.

07:28.360 --> 07:33.110
I guess it's time to really
start thinking about what to do

07:33.200 --> 07:35.570
after Kenji graduates from high school...

07:36.370 --> 07:38.330
How are things with you, Rin?

07:41.250 --> 07:45.080
Do you regret giving up ballet?

07:45.170 --> 07:48.130
No. It's the choice I made.

07:49.710 --> 07:51.090
Grandmother...

07:51.880 --> 07:55.140
I'm sorry for always having the same conversation.

07:58.720 --> 08:00.810
I'm happy to hear your voice.

08:00.890 --> 08:04.980
I'm sure you'll be very busy,
but I hope you'll call again sometime.

08:05.060 --> 08:06.190
Of course I will!

08:06.270 --> 08:08.730
I'll talk to you later. Bye.

08:08.820 --> 08:10.610
Bye.

08:13.030 --> 08:15.740
Rin! Bathroom's all yours!

08:15.820 --> 08:17.200
Oh, okay.

08:18.240 --> 08:19.410
Something the matter?

08:19.740 --> 08:24.080
I'm okay. I guess I'm just tired
after that entrance ceremony.

08:24.170 --> 08:27.000
You should take a shower then. It'll perk you back up.

08:27.090 --> 08:28.290
Yeah!

08:28.380 --> 08:30.340
Listen, Shoko.

08:32.090 --> 08:35.680
I'm glad to be your new roommate as of today!

08:37.930 --> 08:41.890
Same here! I'm glad to be your roommate, too!

08:43.020 --> 08:45.250
But what brought that on? You're so weird, Rin!

08:45.290 --> 08:47.290
Anti-GGP group protests
arrival of aircraft carrier

08:47.310 --> 08:49.690
At today's parade celebrating
the anniversary of the day

08:49.770 --> 08:52.800
the U.N. officially recognized
the GGP's worldwide rule, a group of...

08:53.150 --> 08:56.820
--Umm, you're Rin Ogata, aren't you?
--Huh?

08:56.910 --> 08:59.370
Awesome! It really is you!

08:59.450 --> 09:03.040
I'm Suzuri Uchida!
I'm a first year art student!

09:03.120 --> 09:05.660
I thought it was you!

09:06.080 --> 09:09.380
O-Oh...

09:09.460 --> 09:14.050
It's almost like a dream,
talking to you in person like this!

09:14.130 --> 09:16.050
My mother's a huge fan of yours!

09:16.130 --> 09:19.850
We've seen lots of your performances!

09:19.930 --> 09:22.140
--U-Uhh...
--Do you remember?!

09:22.220 --> 09:24.810
At the Third National Theatre two years ago?!

09:24.890 --> 09:33.110
Oh! Even now, when I close my eyes
I can see your glorious grand jete!

09:33.190 --> 09:35.780
Just thinking about it gives me goose-pimples!

09:35.860 --> 09:39.200
Plus, seeing you up close like this,
you really do look like your mother!

09:39.280 --> 09:43.160
You're the spitting image of
Yuki Ogata, the brilliant dancer!

09:43.250 --> 09:49.290
She was a true, once-in-a-century--
no, once-in-a-millennium-- star!

09:51.000 --> 09:53.880
Then there was that earthquake six years ago...

09:53.960 --> 09:57.970
I cried for days and days after I heard the news...

09:58.840 --> 10:00.260
All right, you! Knock it--

10:00.350 --> 10:02.470
Uemura?

10:02.560 --> 10:05.470
Are you having lunch here too?

10:05.560 --> 10:09.940
What did you choose for your
foreign language? Was it French--?

10:10.020 --> 10:11.440
Ogata...?!

10:11.520 --> 10:13.440
Do you remember me? It's me, Kamiyama!

10:13.530 --> 10:16.400
We made it to the second round of auditions last year!

10:16.490 --> 10:19.910
I thought for sure you'd come here to study theater;

10:19.990 --> 10:22.450
did you really quit ballet?!

10:22.530 --> 10:24.370
Umm...

10:24.450 --> 10:26.080
Rin!

10:26.160 --> 10:28.540
Shouldn't you get going?

10:29.460 --> 10:32.330
You need to sign up for orientation, remember?

10:34.170 --> 10:36.260
S-Sorry! I have to go!

10:36.340 --> 10:38.300
I'll call you!

10:40.470 --> 10:42.800
Hey, Megumi! Over here!

10:42.890 --> 10:43.890
Coming!

10:43.970 --> 10:47.020
--I'll see you later!
--O-Okay.

10:50.100 --> 10:51.190
Umm...

10:51.270 --> 10:53.230
Was that true?

10:54.820 --> 10:58.190
Did she really give up ballet?

10:58.280 --> 11:02.280
I... umm... uhh...

11:10.170 --> 11:12.370
She tore a ligament?

11:12.460 --> 11:16.090
Regine was Rin's first and last leading role.

11:16.170 --> 11:20.590
She hasn't publicly announced it,
but she's given up ballet.

11:20.680 --> 11:24.300
But why? Lots of dancers have gotten over injuries.

11:24.390 --> 11:30.350
Maybe so, but Rin can't dance
as well as she wants anymore.

11:31.270 --> 11:33.600
She was after something different.

11:33.690 --> 11:39.070
Equaling Yuki Ogata was her goal.
But that's impossible now.

11:40.400 --> 11:44.780
I was a big fan of Rin's too, just as big as you...

12:34.540 --> 12:36.710
Excuse me...

13:41.400 --> 13:44.530
That was some thunder, wasn't it?

13:47.070 --> 13:48.490
Sorry for barging in...!

13:48.570 --> 13:51.330
Are you here to join our club?!

13:51.410 --> 13:55.410
Sweet! Welcome to the RideBack club!

13:55.500 --> 14:01.250
Who would've thought that
such a cute, tidy girl would come here!

14:01.340 --> 14:03.250
T-Tidy...?

14:03.340 --> 14:06.260
Oh, I know! Let's go for a ride!

14:06.340 --> 14:09.430
We just got it back from the shop today!

14:09.510 --> 14:12.680
Oh, no, I just wanted to stay out of the rain.

14:12.760 --> 14:15.180
Plus I don't have a license...

14:15.270 --> 14:20.770
That's no problem! You don't need
a special license to ride one of these!

14:20.860 --> 14:25.360
The computer handles all the complicated controls,

14:25.440 --> 14:28.360
so just about anyone can ride one with ease!

14:28.450 --> 14:31.620
They haven't been made street-legal yet, though.

14:31.700 --> 14:34.200
What is it, anyway?

14:34.290 --> 14:37.540
This is a RideBack.
Haven't you seen them on TV before?

14:37.620 --> 14:38.580
No...

14:38.670 --> 14:42.250
Oh. I guess most people haven't heard of 'em yet.

14:43.040 --> 14:46.460
A RideBack is a limbed, two-wheel passenger vehicle.

14:46.550 --> 14:50.470
It's a humanoid motorcycle that can
realize three-dimensional movements

14:50.550 --> 14:52.720
that would be impossible
for normal two-wheel vehicles!

14:52.800 --> 14:55.510
They've been slowly gaining recognition;

14:55.600 --> 14:58.810
there are even national tournaments and stuff.

14:58.890 --> 15:00.350
Oh...

15:00.440 --> 15:04.770
That one is a Mountain Trail RB
manufactured by Teryan Kaduro.

15:04.860 --> 15:09.900
It's a Type L "Fuego." It's Spanish for "fire."

15:10.410 --> 15:11.570
Fuego...

15:11.660 --> 15:14.200
As its name suggests,
it's a rather distinctive model,

15:14.280 --> 15:16.240
but it's simple to control.

15:17.830 --> 15:19.080
Still...

15:19.160 --> 15:23.130
It's still raining out. You should
try getting on it to pass the time!

15:28.590 --> 15:32.630
--Okay, just for a little bit.
--Yes, of course!

15:32.720 --> 15:35.600
Okay, first, you come around from the back...

15:43.610 --> 15:45.560
Is this right?

15:46.690 --> 15:48.110
You're very light on your feet.

15:48.190 --> 15:51.280
Can you scoot forward a little more?

15:51.360 --> 15:53.610
Put your hands on the handles.

15:53.700 --> 15:56.780
Now touch the rectangular screen attached to them.

15:57.740 --> 16:00.700
Uhh... Do you mean this?

16:04.710 --> 16:06.670
Oh, it's going to be shaky.

16:11.880 --> 16:13.300
How does it feel?

16:13.380 --> 16:15.300
This is really high up!

16:15.390 --> 16:16.850
"Ride on back."

16:16.930 --> 16:20.970
Some say it's like being given
a piggyback ride, like the name suggests.

16:24.900 --> 16:27.190
Come here, Fuego.

16:27.270 --> 16:30.480
This Ride... uhh... thingy can talk?!

16:30.570 --> 16:32.490
RideBack.

16:32.570 --> 16:36.870
It can't talk, but it does accept simple commands.

16:37.780 --> 16:39.530
Oh! The rain stopped!

16:39.620 --> 16:41.500
Well, I should go now...

16:41.580 --> 16:46.790
Want to take it for a spin?
Riding a RideBack outside feels great!

16:46.880 --> 16:49.590
Let's switch off battery mode and turn the engine on.

16:51.630 --> 16:55.380
Hey, are you paying attention?

16:55.470 --> 16:56.470
Yes...!

16:56.550 --> 16:59.350
Turn the center key right with your right hand

16:59.430 --> 17:02.390
and press the start button below the red switch.

17:05.650 --> 17:07.600
Turn the right grip...

17:10.780 --> 17:13.900
...and press down on the pedal with your right foot.

17:16.160 --> 17:17.530
Now look forward.

17:19.950 --> 17:22.910
Okay, I'm going to release the lock now.

17:23.750 --> 17:26.580
Slowly let go of the left-hand lever,

17:26.670 --> 17:28.630
ease up with your left hand and right foot,

17:29.000 --> 17:31.420
and slowly turn your right hand...

17:31.500 --> 17:33.840
Yes, just like that.

17:37.470 --> 17:39.390
Nice view, isn't it?

17:39.470 --> 17:42.390
Now grip the left-hand lever again.

17:42.470 --> 17:45.430
Umm, this lever won't budge at all...!

17:46.390 --> 17:48.900
Huh? Then pull the one on the right!

17:48.980 --> 17:51.310
It's no good! They're stuck!

17:51.400 --> 17:52.900
Watch where you're going!

17:52.980 --> 17:54.780
Lean right!

17:55.860 --> 17:57.030
Left!

17:58.450 --> 18:00.370
Nice power-slide!

18:00.450 --> 18:01.740
I mean, oh, no!

18:02.740 --> 18:06.710
S-Stop! Calm down!

18:06.790 --> 18:08.170
It listened...

18:11.000 --> 18:12.040
What is that?

18:12.920 --> 18:16.510
--Man, she's fearless!
--Hey! Your panties are showing!

18:25.140 --> 18:28.520
It responds to however I shift my weight!

18:28.960 --> 18:29.000
Danger ahead

18:39.200 --> 18:41.160
It's so strange! I'm not scared at all!

18:42.740 --> 18:45.540
I feel so at ease! I wonder why...

18:54.460 --> 18:56.510
It can dance!

19:01.760 --> 19:05.060
I'm so close to the cherry blossoms!

19:05.140 --> 19:07.600
Hey, can you do a pirouette next?

19:17.780 --> 19:19.740
H-Hey! What's going on?!

19:28.620 --> 19:32.580
Out practicing RideBack moves,
like always. If anything happens...

19:33.580 --> 19:35.710
Get out of the way!

19:35.800 --> 19:37.420
Sorry! I'll call you back!

19:37.510 --> 19:39.340
Tamayo!

19:39.420 --> 19:42.380
--The Fuego's out of control!
--Let me on! I saw it just now!

19:42.470 --> 19:44.640
--I think it was the control
board's electronics...

19:44.640 --> 19:46.010
--Just hurry.
--I think it was the control
board's electronics...

19:46.100 --> 19:47.260
Hold on!

19:47.770 --> 19:49.720
Isn't that a little too much...?!

19:51.850 --> 19:53.310
This is insane!

19:53.400 --> 19:55.690
But that's more of an aerodynamics thing--

20:04.990 --> 20:06.370
Oh no...!

20:07.740 --> 20:10.040
What are you doing?!
Cut the engine and get off!

20:10.120 --> 20:12.080
I'd like to, but...!

20:16.000 --> 20:20.460
How can I make it stop?
It suddenly stopped listening to me...

20:26.470 --> 20:27.850
Look out!

20:27.930 --> 20:29.390
I'm sorry!

20:34.980 --> 20:36.860
She's headed for...!

20:51.540 --> 20:54.410
Keep your hands on the handles! Look out!

20:56.830 --> 20:58.210
Here comes another!

21:02.050 --> 21:03.510
The road...!

21:10.180 --> 21:12.640
--It's back!
--Brake!

21:12.730 --> 21:14.680
Brake, how?!

21:29.490 --> 21:31.530
--Sh-She jumped!
--No way!

21:33.120 --> 21:34.500
Wow...

21:52.930 --> 21:56.060
<i>The world changes...</i>

21:56.770 --> 22:01.360
Even when he laughs

22:03.400 --> 22:08.780
I'm thinking of you before I realize it

22:12.030 --> 22:16.830
And the hands holding his

22:18.830 --> 22:24.130
feel your warmth, too

22:26.470 --> 22:30.220
Even if I cut out my recollections

22:30.300 --> 22:34.180
and drive them out of my heart

22:34.270 --> 22:37.930
or try to kick the memories out

22:38.020 --> 22:42.400
I still think of you

22:42.480 --> 22:46.900
Time now passes and seasons fly by

22:46.990 --> 22:50.740
Even if that smile starts to become hazy

22:50.820 --> 22:54.740
my heart will never forget you

22:54.830 --> 22:58.500
(even if we can never meet again)

22:58.580 --> 23:02.330
Even if I knock over photos of us smiling

23:02.420 --> 23:06.500
or try to hide my overflowing feelings

23:07.720 --> 23:10.760
my heart will never forget

23:11.680 --> 23:14.850
my memories with you

23:26.110 --> 23:41.100
New Hishida Theatre

23:26.360 --> 23:30.030
Hooray! Tidy girl! We're finally
going to have a lively club, Pres!

23:30.110 --> 23:33.580
Well, excuse me. I guess I'm just
a crude, rusted, iron woman then.

23:33.660 --> 23:35.870
--I'm just a clanky, beat-up--
--Should I order a new RideBack?

23:35.930 --> 23:39.680
Next Episode

23:35.930 --> 23:39.680
Challenge from Tamayo!? S.L.F ~ Spread Legs Form

23:35.990 --> 23:37.330
Huh? What are you holding?

23:37.410 --> 23:39.410
--Let's take this out back.

23:39.410 --> 23:40.790
--Wha...?!
--Let's take this out back.
